__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# `.env` and everything derived from it. `.env` alone left `.env.bak.*`, `.env.save`,
# `.env.local` and an editor's `.env~` committable, and a backup of a secrets file is the
# same secret. `.env.example` is tracked and documents the keys, so it is negated back in.
.env*
!.env.example
# data/* and not data/ — git will not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# `!data/keep-me.csv` under a plain `data/` rule is silently inert. Excluding the
# contents instead is what makes the negations below actually work.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# Documentation, not data.
!data/README.md
# The news pipeline's output is the historical record: a past Wednesday cannot be
# regenerated, so it is tracked despite living under data/.
!data/player_sentiment_*.csv
# The two Mantra artefacts moved to src/fantabot/data/ in P11-6 -- they are the
# matcher's input, so they ship with the package. Not listed here: `data/*` carries a
# slash and is therefore anchored to this file's directory, so it never reached them.
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# `docs/` is tracked from 2026-09-24, except the two third-party binaries under
# `docs/sources/`. Everything here is written in this repository — the FantaLab notes, the
# four specs, the API map — and it was one disk away from gone while ~14 paths under it were
# cited from tracked `src/`. What stays out is not ours to republish from a public repo:
# `Tabella-sostituzioni-per-schema-2024-2025.pdf` is fantacalcio.it's, and
# `leghe-chunk-Dc2l8Fqx.js` is a copy of their minified bundle. Both are backed up at
# `~/.fantabot/docs-sources-backup/` with a `SHA256SUMS.txt`; `docs/sources/README.md` is
# tracked and records their provenance, byte counts and the 403s that make them
# unrecoverable, so the loss is at least legible.
docs/sources/*.pdf
docs/sources/*.js

# Database dumps. scripts/db_dump.sh refuses to write onto this volume at all,
# because a dump carries the league_tokens rows — encrypted, but still
# credentials — and the working tree is one `git add -A` from a commit, now with
# a remote to push it to. A dump asked for in the repo root is ignored instead.
*.dump
*.sql

# The Remotion project behind the full-screen animations in script.md.
# Renders land in out/ and are regenerable: `cd video && npx remotion render <id>`.
video/node_modules/
video/out/

# macOS + local scratch, never publish
.DS_Store
/out/
/script.md
/video/

# maintainer-only, never publish
/SPEC.md

# Task-0 capture tools — throwaway, and they carry the maintainer's own league/room/team
# ids (and a public Firebase web key). Kept local, never committed to a public repo.
scripts/capture_*.py
scripts/read_classic_lineup.py

# Local scratch and live-site captures — hold real DOM/console/PII from leghe.fantacalcio.it.
# Untracked-and-unignored is one `git add -A` from publication; ignore before going public.
.playwright-mcp/
_pdftext.txt

# Per-phase working notes, and the maintainer-only backlog: decided-but-not-done work
# and defects found but not fixed. SPEC.md is already ignored (line 48); plan.md/todo.md
# are its siblings and get archived to tasks/archive/ on phase close, not committed.
#
# No trailing slash, deliberately, and the reason is a record rather than the current
# state. `tasks/` matches a *directory* only. `tasks` was once a symlink to
# ~/.fantabot/tasks — which git treats as a file, so the slashed pattern missed it
# entirely and `git status` reported `?? tasks` while `git clean -xfd` offered to remove
# the only pointer to the record. Today (2026-09-24) `tasks` is a plain directory in the
# tree and ~/.fantabot/tasks no longer exists, so the slashed form would work again; the
# unslashed one covers both shapes and is kept for that reason. It is ignored either way
# because `origin` is public and the notes carry FantaLab platform findings, both league
# ids and unfixed defects on the acting path.
tasks
todo
